diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce the reported outage. End-to-end connectivity from Office A to the Office B server segment is healthy.

Evidence:
- From PC1 (10.1.0.100), ping to the server (10.5.0.4) succeeds with 0% loss and low RTT (~2 ms). Reverse ping from the server (srv1) to PC1 is also 0% loss.
- A basic application probe from PC1 (HTTP GET to 10.5.0.4) completes immediately, indicating L3/L4 reachability and fast response.
- Routing/control plane looks normal in the core: on csw1, all OSPF neighbors are Full (to its WAN peer and to distribution/core links), so the inter-site routing fabric is up.
- Endpoints are configured correctly: PC1 has default via 10.1.0.1; srv1 has default via 10.5.0.1 and is in 10.5.0.0/24.

Affected component: none observed (routing and data-plane).
Mechanism: Because both ICMP and a TCP-based probe succeed bidirectionally, the inter-site path through the OSPF core is functioning; an actual core/link failure would show loss or asymmetric reachability.
Localization: Verified at endpoints (PC1, srv1) and at core control plane (csw1 OSPF neighbors).
Root cause: Not present now; the issue is not reproducible with current evidence.
Corrective fix: No restart recommended. If users still report issues, capture a traceroute from an affected host during the event and review FRR logs (csw1/csw2) for flaps around the reported time to pinpoint any transient reconvergence or interface events.
